+## GLM prompt chunk rows (TF_GLM_PREFILL_ROWS)
+
+`families/glm5_next/cuda/engine.py`'s `prefill_rows_from_env` (TF_GLM_PREFILL_ROWS: the rows a prompt chunk runs at
+once, a multiple of 64 from 64 to 16,384; 2,048 when unset) and `cuda/geometry.py`'s `mla_geometry(prefill_rows=)` and
+`mla_chunk_scratch(prefill_rows=)` (the estimate's prompt-chunk terms at the chunk's rows) are ported from MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/1576746)
+patches 0004-glm-prompt-kernels and 0008-glm-prompt-grid (her `GlmEngine` reads the switch; her geometry takes the
+rows), Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab (see [the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). Changes in the
+port: the engine reads the switch before its startup estimate, so that the estimate counts the chunk's buffers, the
+fp8 indexer rings and the pairs' second chunk (TF_GLM_PREFILL_PAIRS, in flight under TF_GLM_MCDMA_INFLIGHT) at these
+rows, and the AFD attention node reads it before the expert wire opens; the expert nodes size their scratch and wire
+slots off the settings handshake's `prefill_rows` as before, and an MCDMA mailbox too small for a chunk is refused at
+startup (`check_room`); a value passed as `GlmEngine(prefill_rows=)` is taken as given. Unset, the estimate, the
+buffers and the calls are the ones before.
